            <ArticleTitle>Foetal dilated cardiomyopathy with left ventricular thrombosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1191-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S104795111500027X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serial foetal echocardiography showed the development of severe left ventricular systolic dysfunction and thrombosis in a previously healthy foetus. Normal cardiac findings in a mid-trimester foetus do not exclude subsequent dilated cardiomyopathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
